{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> \"Like a river I will extend to Zion peace, and like a wadi flooding the wealth of nations shall come\" — like \"for He has done me this wealth\" (Deuteronomy 8:17)." "<b>On the side you shall be carried.</b> At the time you come from exile." "<b>You shall be dandled.</b> Like \"and the suckling shall dandle\" (Isaiah 11:8), and the ayin comes with kamatz chataf because it is at the end of a verse."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {2 "Hebrew text reads 'העין' ('the eye'); by context this refers to the letter ayin in the word תשעשעו. Translated hyper-literally as 'the ayin.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:14.746479131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}